  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan receives a polite invitation signed with Man tribe leader Man Tu’s name. At the meeting Man Tu greets him deeply, scolds Man Duo, and trades praise with the man he believes to be Wolf King Chang Shan Yin. Fang Yuan names him ruler of near a thousand Gu Masters, controller of Hong Yan valley, and peak stage where Fang Yuan’s cultivation has fallen to rank four initial stage.",
      "chapters": [
        445
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_man_tribe",
        "char_man_duo",
        "char_chang_shan_yin",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "loc_hong_yan_valley"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is nine feet tall, extremely muscular and strong. He wears a loose sleeveless fur robe that shows his shoulders. His ancient-bronze colored arms are thicker than a normal male’s leg.",
      "chapters": [
        445
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He supports Man Duo’s push to marry Ge Yao while also eyeing Ge tribe. After Ge Yao’s death is treated as settled he tells Man Duo that C grade aptitude bars succession and that Man Duo must assist his elder brother.",
      "chapters": [
        448
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ge-yao-and-ge-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ge_yao",
        "fac_ge_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When the wolf lure plan fails and Ge Guang succeeds the Ge tribe leader seat, Man Tu refuses to mobilize the tribe without a public excuse and keeps luring wolves to harm Ge tribe while blaming Chang Shan Yin for Man tribe’s loss.",
      "chapters": [
        458
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ge-yao-and-ge-tribe",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ge_guang"
      ]
    }
  ],
